# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Only checked when no real static
# file matches the request path first (Cloudflare's own precedence,
# real files like /assets/*.js, /admin.html, /manifest.json always win
# over these rules automatically, no rule needed for those).

# /admin already works via Cloudflare's automatic "strip .html"
# behavior alone, no rule needed here for it. A real, confirmed
# production bug (found by directly curling the live site, not by
# browser testing, which had only ever hit localhost until now): an
# explicit rule here that rewrites /admin -> /admin.html actively
# FIGHTS that same automatic behavior, Cloudflare's own platform-level
# ".html stripping" redirect intercepts the rewrite's internal fetch
# of /admin.html and 308s it right back to /admin, which re-triggers
# this rule again, forever, an infinite redirect loop
# (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS in a real browser). Do not re-add a rule
# here for /admin, the automatic behavior already covers it correctly
# on its own.

# Everything else (a short ride slug like /08112026, or any future
# path) serves index.html instead of a 404, letting src/main.ts read
# the real path itself (see getRideIdFromUrl()) and look up the ride.
/*       /index.html   200
